/-
# Largest and smallest totient preimages (Erdős Problem 694)

Erdős Problem 694: let `f_max(n)` be the largest `m` such that `φ(m) = n`, and `f_min(n)` be the
smallest such `m`, where `φ` is Euler's totient function. Investigate `max_{n ≤ x} f_max(n) /
f_min(n)` (where the maximum is restricted to those `n` of the form `n = φ(m)` for some `m`).
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Data.Nat.Totient
public import Mathlib.NumberTheory.Harmonic.EulerMascheroni

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.NumberTheory.TotientPreimageRatioErdosProblem694Wanted

/-!
Source: T. F. Bloom, Erdős Problems, Problem #694, https://www.erdosproblems.com/694 (status SOLVED
(LEAN)). UnsolvedMath record UM-00002263 (`EP-694`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The preimage `φ⁻¹(n)` is finite and nonempty for the admissible `n ≥ 1`, so `sSup`/`sInf` are its
largest and smallest elements; the maximum over `1 ≤ n ≤ x` is the `sSup` of a finite nonempty set
of reals for `x ≥ 1`. "Investigate" is answered by the asymptotic recorded on the problem page,
stated as a limit of the ratio to `log log x`. The proof is machine-generated (GPT-5.5 Pro); the
problem page marks the problem solved. Compared with the formal-conjectures statement
`ErdosProblems/694.lean` (equivalent; no code imported).
-/

open Filter Topology

/-- For `n` in the image of Euler's totient `φ`, `f_max(n) / f_min(n)`: the ratio of the largest
and the smallest `m` with `φ(m) = n` (the preimage is finite and nonempty for such `n ≥ 1`). -/
noncomputable def totientPreimageRatio (n : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ((sSup (Nat.totient ⁻¹' {n}) : ℕ) : ℝ) / ((sInf (Nat.totient ⁻¹' {n}) : ℕ) : ℝ)

/-- `max_{n ≤ x} f_max(n) / f_min(n)`, the maximum over the `n ≤ x` of the form `n = φ(m)`,
`n ≥ 1` (a finite nonempty set of values for `x ≥ 1`, since `φ(1) = 1`). -/
noncomputable def maxTotientPreimageRatio (x : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  sSup (totientPreimageRatio '' {n : ℕ | 1 ≤ n ∧ n ≤ x ∧ ∃ m, Nat.totient m = n})

/-- Erdős Problem 694, as resolved: `max_{n ≤ x} f_max(n) / f_min(n) = (e^γ + o(1)) log log x`,
`γ` the Euler-Mascheroni constant. -/
def maxTotientPreimageRatioAsymptotic : Prop :=
  Tendsto (fun x : ℕ => maxTotientPreimageRatio x / Real.log (Real.log x)) atTop
    (𝓝 (Real.exp Real.eulerMascheroniConstant))

/--
Resolved: erdosproblems.com/694 records a proof (generated by GPT-5.5 Pro, prompted by Price) that
`max_{n ≤ x} f_max(n) / f_min(n) = (e^γ + o(1)) log log x`, `γ` the Euler-Mascheroni constant, and
lists the problem as solved. Source: T. F. Bloom, Erdős Problems, Problem #694,
https://www.erdosproblems.com/694 (status SOLVED (LEAN)); resolution: GPT-5.5 Pro (prompted by L.
Price), proof posted at https://www.overleaf.com/read/fgmhvywvdjkt (2026), recorded on
erdosproblems.com/694, erdosproblems.com/694: max_{n ≤ x} f_max(n) / f_min(n) = (e^γ + o(1)) log log
x; status SOLVED (LEAN), https://www.erdosproblems.com/694.
-/
public theorem_wanted maxTotientPreimageRatioAsymptotic_holds : maxTotientPreimageRatioAsymptotic

end MathlibExt.NumberTheory.TotientPreimageRatioErdosProblem694Wanted
